        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive collection requirement built out for monitoring coup risk across Coastal West Africa, specifically driven by the spillover dynamics from Sahel instability documented in this year's threat assessment. The requirement should task HUMINT, OSINT, and SIGINT equities to track civil-military tensions, public dissatisfaction indicators, and engagement by foreign partners who may be willing to tolerate or encourage military takeovers in exchange for narrow security cooperation. Collection should cover at minimum Ghana, Togo, Benin, and C\u00f4te d'Ivoire, with reporting priority weighted toward states where governance deficits most closely mirror pre-coup conditions seen in Sahel states since 2020. We also need indicators and warnings for scenarios where aspiring coup leaders assess that major-power competition gives them enough diplomatic space to survive international pressure post-seizure. Please incorporate linkages to the unresolved Ethiopia-Amhara-Tigray situation as a contextual analogue for how frozen conflicts and militia dynamics can destabilize neighboring regions. Reporting cadence should be weekly summary cables with flash reporting for any imminent threat indicators. Coordinate nominations through the National HUMINT Requirements Tasking Center and ensure OSINT feeds are ingested into COLISEUM. Final collection plan is needed by close of business next Friday for review at the Africa Issues Managers meeting.",
